1
00:00:01,074 --> 00:00:01,925
On day 301,

2
00:00:01,925 --> 00:00:04,709
Wes peels the tape off the switch.

3
00:00:05,083 --> 00:00:06,520
Nobody has slept.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,797
At first light,

5
00:00:07,797 --> 00:00:11,471
the radio crackles, and Ansel is still whispering.

6
00:00:11,471 --> 00:00:12,604
"They came over the

7
00:00:12,604 --> 00:00:14,267
fields in the night," he says.

8
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:16,292
"They're on the bridge again.

9
00:00:16,292 --> 00:00:17,536
They're in the streets.

10
00:00:17,536 --> 00:00:19,703
They're standing under our windows."

11
00:00:20,253 --> 00:00:21,078
A breath.

12
00:00:21,078 --> 00:00:22,727
"We're all upstairs.

13
00:00:22,727 --> 00:00:24,016
We're fine.

14
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:27,067
But the spring is on the other side of them,

15
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:29,487
and we have water for nine days."

16
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,414
Your name is Patch.

17
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:33,116
Three hundred days ago,

18
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:35,782
you were waiting for a bus.

19
00:00:36,124 --> 00:00:38,976
Since then, you have lived under a bus

20
00:00:38,976 --> 00:00:41,651
depot with Nora, Wes and Vera,

21
00:00:41,651 --> 00:00:45,798
and for the last month with three people from the sea:

22
00:00:45,798 --> 00:00:48,048
Ruth in her yellow raincoat,

23
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:52,542
Kit in his white helmet, and Bram, who doesn't talk.

24
00:00:52,542 --> 00:00:54,479
A month ago, you put a few

25
00:00:54,479 --> 00:00:56,536
thousand of the dead in a gravel

26
00:00:56,536 --> 00:00:58,546
pit and closed a gate on them.

27
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,201
Then it rained.

28
00:01:00,201 --> 00:01:01,461
And this morning,

29
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:05,141
they are standing under the windows of nineteen people who

30
00:01:05,141 --> 00:01:07,983
were finally allowed to stop whispering.

31
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:10,178
Wes doesn't say anything.

32
00:01:10,632 --> 00:01:13,340
He just walks across the yard to the canopy,

33
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,570
climbs the ladder,

34
00:01:14,570 --> 00:01:16,651
and stands under the loudspeaker,

35
00:01:16,651 --> 00:01:21,089
with its switch taped on OFF since day 239.

36
00:01:21,703 --> 00:01:23,005
He picks at the corner of

37
00:01:23,005 --> 00:01:24,458
the tape with his thumbnail.

38
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:26,168
Then he pulls it off,

39
00:01:26,168 --> 00:01:30,228
all in one long strip, and sticks it to his own sleeve,

40
00:01:30,228 --> 00:01:31,906
so he doesn't lose it.

41
00:01:31,906 --> 00:01:33,286
"It's on the list of

42
00:01:33,286 --> 00:01:35,432
things I'm sorry about," he says.

43
00:01:35,432 --> 00:01:37,121
"Might as well be on the

44
00:01:37,121 --> 00:01:38,835
list of things I'm not."

45
00:01:38,835 --> 00:01:42,231
On day 302, you ask the question again.

46
00:01:42,765 --> 00:01:44,914
"Where do we take them?"

47
00:01:44,914 --> 00:01:45,848
Not away.

48
00:01:45,848 --> 00:01:48,489
Away is just somebody else's door.

49
00:01:48,489 --> 00:01:50,887
You have learned that twice now.

50
00:01:51,516 --> 00:01:53,863
Ruth spreads the road map on the bench.

51
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:56,108
Ansel's pencil circle by the sea.

52
00:01:56,108 --> 00:01:58,130
Her own thin line to it.

53
00:01:58,551 --> 00:02:01,517
Fields, towns, motorways, rivers.

54
00:02:01,517 --> 00:02:04,275
Bram looks at it for a long time,

55
00:02:04,275 --> 00:02:05,572
and whistles two notes.

56
00:02:05,572 --> 00:02:07,701
"Not the pit," says Vera.

57
00:02:07,701 --> 00:02:09,593
"It's got two doors now."

58
00:02:09,593 --> 00:02:11,990
"Not the sea," says Ruth.

59
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:14,662
"Two days at their speed is two weeks.

60
00:02:14,662 --> 00:02:17,258
And then they'd be on our beach."

61
00:02:17,258 --> 00:02:19,058
You look at the map.

62
00:02:19,058 --> 00:02:21,431
Then you look up, at the yard around you.

63
00:02:21,806 --> 00:02:23,116
The high walls.

64
00:02:23,116 --> 00:02:24,262
The one gate.

65
00:02:24,262 --> 00:02:26,903
The canopy, the loudspeaker.

66
00:02:26,903 --> 00:02:28,744
The dark rectangle where the

67
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:30,535
coach stood for seven months,

68
00:02:30,535 --> 00:02:33,113
with eleven passengers inside it.

69
00:02:33,552 --> 00:02:34,862
You lived under the

70
00:02:34,862 --> 00:02:36,472
river for two hundred days.

71
00:02:37,152 --> 00:02:38,653
You know exactly how many

72
00:02:38,653 --> 00:02:40,687
of them this yard can hold.

73
00:02:40,687 --> 00:02:41,701
All of them.

74
00:02:41,701 --> 00:02:43,170
"Here," you say.

75
00:02:43,673 --> 00:02:44,767
Nobody answers.

76
00:02:44,767 --> 00:02:45,999
Nora looks at the

77
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:48,187
bunker door for a long time.

78
00:02:48,187 --> 00:02:51,685
"It's got one way in," says Vera, at last.

79
00:02:51,685 --> 00:02:53,040
"And we know how to

80
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,581
live under it," says Wes.

81
00:02:55,581 --> 00:02:57,055
"No," you say.

82
00:02:57,055 --> 00:02:58,551
"Not this time.

83
00:02:58,551 --> 00:03:01,416
This time, we give them the yard.

84
00:03:01,416 --> 00:03:04,150
And we go and live somewhere with a view."

85
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:06,222
Nora finally looks at you.

86
00:03:06,222 --> 00:03:07,916
Then she nods, once,

87
00:03:07,916 --> 00:03:11,144
the way she nods when something is decided and there

88
00:03:11,144 --> 00:03:14,114
is no point talking about it anymore.

89
00:03:14,114 --> 00:03:17,055
From day 303 to day 305,

90
00:03:17,055 --> 00:03:18,645
you empty the bunker.

91
00:03:18,645 --> 00:03:21,417
The hill people come down with handcarts,

92
00:03:21,417 --> 00:03:23,117
and everything you own goes

93
00:03:23,117 --> 00:03:25,974
up the hill road, one load at a time.

94
00:03:25,974 --> 00:03:27,267
The tins.

95
00:03:27,267 --> 00:03:28,246
The blankets.

96
00:03:28,246 --> 00:03:29,366
The jump leads.

97
00:03:29,366 --> 00:03:31,682
The radio from the shelf.

98
00:03:31,682 --> 00:03:33,076
The rope on the bolt stays

99
00:03:33,076 --> 00:03:33,747
where it is,

100
00:03:33,747 --> 00:03:36,795
because you are going to need it one last time.

101
00:03:36,795 --> 00:03:39,096
Nora goes to the locker room alone.

102
00:03:39,454 --> 00:03:42,320
She comes back with the postcard and the road map,

103
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:43,725
folded together,

104
00:03:43,725 --> 00:03:46,674
and puts them in the very bottom of the turquoise bag.

105
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,010
She leaves the locker door open.

106
00:03:49,010 --> 00:03:51,477
Wes stands in front of the chart on

107
00:03:51,477 --> 00:03:53,022
the bunker wall with a piece of

108
00:03:53,022 --> 00:03:56,273
cardboard and a pencil, copying the totals.

109
00:03:56,273 --> 00:03:56,833
Days.

110
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,442
Zombies gone.

111
00:03:59,137 --> 00:04:00,251
People met.

112
00:04:00,251 --> 00:04:01,922
Days in daylight.

113
00:04:01,922 --> 00:04:04,331
When he gets to the bottom,

114
00:04:04,331 --> 00:04:05,788
he writes one more line.

115
00:04:05,788 --> 00:04:08,709
"Moved house," he reads out.

116
00:04:08,709 --> 00:04:10,069
"Day 305."

117
00:04:10,668 --> 00:04:11,798
You don't take much

118
00:04:11,798 --> 00:04:13,266
from the bunker yourself.

119
00:04:13,266 --> 00:04:14,933
Just the orange bag.

120
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:16,848
It has everything in it already.

121
00:04:16,848 --> 00:04:18,357
On the way up the stairs,

122
00:04:18,357 --> 00:04:22,199
you stop at the steel door and put your hand flat on it,

123
00:04:22,199 --> 00:04:25,334
once, the way Bram listens to concrete.

124
00:04:25,334 --> 00:04:26,130
It's cold.

125
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:27,282
It always was.

126
00:04:27,282 --> 00:04:29,410
On the last night, the seven of you

127
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:31,705
sleep in the bunker together,

128
00:04:31,705 --> 00:04:33,332
shoulder to shoulder on the floor,

129
00:04:33,332 --> 00:04:35,735
with Bram sitting up against the steel door.

130
00:04:35,735 --> 00:04:37,797
Nora turns the lantern down,

131
00:04:37,797 --> 00:04:40,503
the way she has every night for

132
00:04:40,503 --> 00:04:41,621
three hundred and five nights.

133
00:04:41,979 --> 00:04:43,358
Then, for the first time,

134
00:04:43,358 --> 00:04:45,249
she turns it all the way off.

135
00:04:45,736 --> 00:04:48,867
On day 306, you drive to the city.

136
00:04:48,867 --> 00:04:49,990
Three of you go.

137
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:51,240
You drive.

138
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:52,988
Vera sits beside you,

139
00:04:52,988 --> 00:04:56,187
because nobody knows the roads to the city better.

140
00:04:56,187 --> 00:04:57,508
Bram sits by the window,

141
00:04:57,508 --> 00:05:00,187
because if anything goes wrong with the truck,

142
00:05:00,187 --> 00:05:03,369
Bram is the one who will fix it, without a word.

143
00:05:03,824 --> 00:05:05,448
Wes stays on the canopy roof,

144
00:05:05,448 --> 00:05:07,828
with the microphone on its long cable.

145
00:05:07,828 --> 00:05:10,994
Nora stays on the gantry, with the rope.

146
00:05:10,994 --> 00:05:13,194
Ruth and Kit stay on the hill,

147
00:05:13,194 --> 00:05:15,472
with the radio and the mirror.

148
00:05:15,472 --> 00:05:18,464
And the gate stands wide open behind you,

149
00:05:18,464 --> 00:05:21,192
the way it hasn't stood since day one.

150
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:24,418
You drive out under the sign.

151
00:05:24,418 --> 00:05:25,506
FOUR ALIVE.

152
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,397
For the first time,

153
00:05:27,397 --> 00:05:31,640
the sign is wrong in a way that makes you smile.

154
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:34,376
On day 307, the city is full again.

155
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:36,836
You come over the last rise of the

156
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:38,792
motorway at dawn, and there it is.

157
00:05:38,792 --> 00:05:39,875
The junction.

158
00:05:40,554 --> 00:05:43,564
The bridge, black from railing to railing.

159
00:05:43,564 --> 00:05:45,530
The slip road, black.

160
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:49,137
And beyond them, the edge of the city,

161
00:05:49,137 --> 00:05:50,146
the empty streets,

162
00:05:50,146 --> 00:05:52,357
all filled up again with the dead,

163
00:05:52,357 --> 00:05:55,637
standing in rows like people waiting for news.

164
00:05:55,637 --> 00:05:58,751
On the corner, the tall, narrow house.

165
00:05:58,751 --> 00:06:01,591
In the top window, a lamp is lit.

166
00:06:01,591 --> 00:06:04,460
"They put it back," says Vera quietly.

167
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:06,456
You stop the truck at the

168
00:06:06,456 --> 00:06:07,769
bottom of the slip road,

169
00:06:07,769 --> 00:06:10,962
exactly where the coach stood on day 254.

170
00:06:10,962 --> 00:06:13,154
You roll the window down.

171
00:06:13,512 --> 00:06:15,866
And you put your hand on the horn.

172
00:06:15,866 --> 00:06:16,606
Not short.

173
00:06:16,606 --> 00:06:17,309
Long.

174
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,503
The whole city turns.

175
00:06:19,503 --> 00:06:22,219
It's like watching the tide turn.

176
00:06:22,753 --> 00:06:24,569
First the ones on the bridge,

177
00:06:24,569 --> 00:06:27,820
then the slip road, then street after street,

178
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:30,117
faces lifting, bodies turning,

179
00:06:30,117 --> 00:06:33,455
all at once, toward the one sound in the world.

180
00:06:33,455 --> 00:06:36,197
Up in the top window, a long coat and

181
00:06:36,197 --> 00:06:39,508
a yellow mitten press against the glass.

182
00:06:39,508 --> 00:06:41,515
Ansel lifts one hand.

183
00:06:41,515 --> 00:06:42,610
Then the green one.

184
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:44,089
At the front of the river,

185
00:06:44,089 --> 00:06:46,013
coming down the slip road first,

186
00:06:46,013 --> 00:06:49,008
are two figures you would know anywhere.

187
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:51,702
A navy depot vest with two pockets.

188
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:54,919
And an olive one, one step behind.

189
00:06:54,919 --> 00:06:57,331
"Of course," says Vera.

190
00:06:57,331 --> 00:06:58,574
"Of course it's them."

191
00:06:58,574 --> 00:07:01,357
The radio on the dashboard crackles.

192
00:07:01,357 --> 00:07:03,322
Ansel, not whispering anymore.

193
00:07:03,322 --> 00:07:06,003
"Don't hurry on our account," he says.

194
00:07:06,003 --> 00:07:07,154
"We've waited a week.

195
00:07:07,154 --> 00:07:09,319
We can wait while you turn round."

196
00:07:09,853 --> 00:07:11,633
"We're not turning round," says Vera.

197
00:07:11,633 --> 00:07:13,119
"We're taking them home."

198
00:07:13,845 --> 00:07:14,577
A pause.

199
00:07:14,577 --> 00:07:15,552
"Whose home?"

200
00:07:15,552 --> 00:07:18,060
You look at the long black river

201
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,493
coming down the slip road toward you.

202
00:07:21,138 --> 00:07:22,404
"Ours," you say.

203
00:07:22,404 --> 00:07:25,180
From day 308 to day 312,

204
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:26,871
you lead them home.

205
00:07:26,871 --> 00:07:30,089
At the speed of a very slow queue.

206
00:07:30,089 --> 00:07:32,833
One long blast every few minutes.

207
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:35,260
The truck crawls back down the motorway

208
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,015
you have driven three times now,

209
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:39,418
with the river walking behind it,

210
00:07:39,418 --> 00:07:44,098
filling every lane, kilometer after kilometer of the dead,

211
00:07:44,695 --> 00:07:47,477
all following the same white truck home.

212
00:07:47,477 --> 00:07:49,995
At night, you stop on the empty

213
00:07:49,995 --> 00:07:51,596
side of the central barrier,

214
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,205
and turn the engine off,

215
00:07:53,205 --> 00:07:56,345
and the river stops behind you and waits.

216
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:58,782
Bram sleeps sitting up.

217
00:07:58,782 --> 00:08:00,674
Vera sleeps sitting up.

218
00:08:01,101 --> 00:08:04,042
You don't sleep much at all.

219
00:08:04,042 --> 00:08:06,656
On day 309, the truck's engine starts

220
00:08:06,656 --> 00:08:09,233
coughing on the long hill after the bridge,

221
00:08:09,233 --> 00:08:11,416
and the river catches up until the

222
00:08:11,416 --> 00:08:14,097
first hands are nearly on the tailgate.

223
00:08:14,097 --> 00:08:15,610
Bram gets out,

224
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:19,338
lifts the bonnet, does something with one finger and a

225
00:08:19,338 --> 00:08:22,292
strip of Wes's tape, and gets back in.

226
00:08:22,292 --> 00:08:24,552
The engine stops coughing.

227
00:08:24,552 --> 00:08:25,946
Bram whistles three

228
00:08:25,946 --> 00:08:28,428
notes and goes back to sleep.

229
00:08:28,428 --> 00:08:29,832
Every sunset,

230
00:08:30,206 --> 00:08:32,118
Ansel comes on the radio.

231
00:08:32,118 --> 00:08:34,397
"Spring's ours," he says.

232
00:08:34,397 --> 00:08:35,498
"Bridge is ours."

233
00:08:35,498 --> 00:08:38,069
And now, after the second night,

234
00:08:38,492 --> 00:08:41,085
"Thank you," every single time,

235
00:08:41,085 --> 00:08:45,394
as if he is afraid you will stop if he forgets.

236
00:08:45,394 --> 00:08:46,663
On day 310,

237
00:08:46,663 --> 00:08:49,129
the truck passes a field you recognize.

238
00:08:49,129 --> 00:08:50,822
Frost has turned into mud,

239
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,593
and the mud has turned green

240
00:08:52,593 --> 00:08:54,713
at the edges, but you know it.

241
00:08:54,713 --> 00:08:56,284
Vera knows it too.

242
00:08:56,284 --> 00:08:57,919
She makes you stop,

243
00:08:57,919 --> 00:09:01,837
and gets out, and walks into the field in her long grey scarf,

244
00:09:01,837 --> 00:09:02,997
a hundred meters ahead

245
00:09:02,997 --> 00:09:05,692
of the river, without hurrying once.

246
00:09:05,692 --> 00:09:07,035
She comes back with

247
00:09:07,035 --> 00:09:10,214
something small and dirty in her hand.

248
00:09:10,214 --> 00:09:11,825
A travel alarm clock.

249
00:09:11,825 --> 00:09:13,701
"It stopped," she says.

250
00:09:13,701 --> 00:09:15,552
She winds it, carefully,

251
00:09:15,552 --> 00:09:19,481
sitting in the cab, while the river catches up behind you.

252
00:09:19,481 --> 00:09:21,102
And it starts to tick.

253
00:09:21,588 --> 00:09:25,760
From day 313 to day 315,

254
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:28,879
you cross the viaduct.

255
00:09:29,205 --> 00:09:31,546
The same viaduct where you

256
00:09:31,546 --> 00:09:34,480
spent the night of day 216,

257
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:37,144
with Vera in the cab for the first time.

258
00:09:37,144 --> 00:09:40,220
You stop at the top of it on day 313,

259
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:44,406
and the river fills the whole long bridge behind you,

260
00:09:44,406 --> 00:09:45,307
end to end,

261
00:09:45,307 --> 00:09:49,517
and stands there, in the dark, waiting for the next horn.

262
00:09:49,972 --> 00:09:50,659
That night,

263
00:09:50,659 --> 00:09:53,306
Nora comes on the radio from the gantry.

264
00:09:53,617 --> 00:09:55,757
"Still here," she says.

265
00:09:55,757 --> 00:09:58,546
"Still here," you say.

266
00:09:58,546 --> 00:10:01,292
"Still here," says Vera,

267
00:10:01,292 --> 00:10:04,418
from beside you, which she has never done before.

268
00:10:04,841 --> 00:10:07,337
There is a long silence on the other end.

269
00:10:07,337 --> 00:10:09,178
Then Nora's voice comes back,

270
00:10:09,178 --> 00:10:11,404
and it doesn't sound quite steady.

271
00:10:12,051 --> 00:10:13,889
"Two more days," she says.

272
00:10:13,889 --> 00:10:15,627
"The yard's ready."

273
00:10:16,628 --> 00:10:20,177
On day 316, the depot calls them home.

274
00:10:20,177 --> 00:10:21,519
You come down off the main

275
00:10:21,519 --> 00:10:22,265
road at midday,

276
00:10:22,265 --> 00:10:25,126
with the whole river strung out behind you.

277
00:10:25,126 --> 00:10:27,017
Half a kilometer from the depot,

278
00:10:27,017 --> 00:10:29,438
the hill road climbs away to the left,

279
00:10:29,438 --> 00:10:30,937
and that's where the plan

280
00:10:30,937 --> 00:10:33,086
says the truck has to leave them.

281
00:10:33,086 --> 00:10:35,921
You take one long look in the mirror.

282
00:10:35,921 --> 00:10:36,857
The navy vest.

283
00:10:36,857 --> 00:10:38,402
The olive vest.

284
00:10:38,402 --> 00:10:40,619
And behind them, thousands.

285
00:10:40,619 --> 00:10:42,830
Then you switch the engine off,

286
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:46,108
and let the truck roll silently up the hill road,

287
00:10:46,108 --> 00:10:48,017
and the river stops behind you,

288
00:10:48,017 --> 00:10:50,025
all of it, on the main road,

289
00:10:50,025 --> 00:10:53,039
facing nowhere, waiting for the next sound.

290
00:10:53,718 --> 00:10:56,327
On the radio, you say one word.

291
00:10:56,327 --> 00:10:57,035
"Now."

292
00:10:57,825 --> 00:11:00,491
And on the canopy, Wes reaches down over

293
00:11:00,491 --> 00:11:03,483
the edge and switches on the loudspeaker.

294
00:11:03,483 --> 00:11:04,431
It crackles.

295
00:11:04,431 --> 00:11:05,387
It hums.

296
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:08,020
And then Wes's voice comes out of it,

297
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:10,293
rolling down the street and over the

298
00:11:10,293 --> 00:11:12,120
walls and across the fields,

299
00:11:12,558 --> 00:11:15,198
louder than anything you have heard in months.

300
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,627
"Passengers for Platform 1," says Wes.

301
00:11:18,627 --> 00:11:20,967
"This is your last call.

302
00:11:20,967 --> 00:11:23,328
Last call for Platform 1."

303
00:11:24,103 --> 00:11:24,978
On day 316,

304
00:11:24,978 --> 00:11:27,892
the river comes back to the yard.

305
00:11:27,892 --> 00:11:29,864
The way it came in on day 90.

306
00:11:29,864 --> 00:11:32,135
Down the street, all of it.

307
00:11:32,135 --> 00:11:33,932
The first ones walk through the open

308
00:11:33,932 --> 00:11:36,737
gate as if they've just come home from work.

309
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:37,391
Then more.

310
00:11:37,391 --> 00:11:39,174
Then the yard starts to fill,

311
00:11:39,174 --> 00:11:41,127
from the back wall forward,

312
00:11:41,127 --> 00:11:44,625
the way a bathtub fills, slow and certain.

313
00:11:44,625 --> 00:11:45,844
Around the canopy.

314
00:11:45,844 --> 00:11:47,877
Around the dark rectangle.

315
00:11:48,203 --> 00:11:49,858
Around the cold fire.

316
00:11:49,858 --> 00:11:51,588
Wes keeps talking.

317
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:54,361
"Please have your tickets ready.

318
00:11:54,361 --> 00:11:56,119
Please mind the gap."

319
00:11:56,638 --> 00:11:58,175
He tells them the weather.

320
00:11:58,175 --> 00:11:59,256
He tells them that

321
00:11:59,256 --> 00:12:01,861
management apologizes for the delay.

322
00:12:01,861 --> 00:12:03,623
He tells them the sad story of

323
00:12:03,623 --> 00:12:06,052
a man who once lived on a roof.

324
00:12:06,052 --> 00:12:07,588
His voice gets hoarse.

325
00:12:07,588 --> 00:12:08,957
He keeps going.

326
00:12:09,557 --> 00:12:11,009
On the gantry over the gate,

327
00:12:11,009 --> 00:12:14,050
Nora holds the rope of the gate bolt in both hands.

328
00:12:14,050 --> 00:12:16,275
They keep coming all afternoon,

329
00:12:16,275 --> 00:12:19,410
until the yard is fuller than it ever was,

330
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:22,180
wall to wall, the way it was in the winter,

331
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:23,907
when you lived under them.

332
00:12:23,907 --> 00:12:25,543
And then there are only

333
00:12:25,543 --> 00:12:27,074
two left in the street.

334
00:12:27,074 --> 00:12:30,112
The night driver walks through the gate.

335
00:12:30,112 --> 00:12:31,206
The Doorman doesn't.

336
00:12:31,206 --> 00:12:33,253
He stops right in the gateway,

337
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:35,615
exactly where he has always stood,

338
00:12:35,615 --> 00:12:38,915
and puts both hands flat on the open gate.

339
00:12:38,915 --> 00:12:41,329
The way he did on day 67.

340
00:12:41,703 --> 00:12:43,537
The way he did all winter.

341
00:12:43,537 --> 00:12:45,212
He has never been on the

342
00:12:45,212 --> 00:12:47,135
inside of this gate in his life.

343
00:12:47,135 --> 00:12:49,091
And the gate can't close

344
00:12:49,091 --> 00:12:50,530
with him standing in it.

345
00:12:50,530 --> 00:12:52,943
The loudspeaker calls and calls.

346
00:12:52,943 --> 00:12:54,145
He doesn't move.

347
00:12:54,145 --> 00:12:55,205
On the gantry,

348
00:12:55,205 --> 00:12:58,419
Nora leans over the edge, right above him.

349
00:12:58,419 --> 00:12:59,720
And she does something

350
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,594
nobody ever taught her.

351
00:13:01,594 --> 00:13:03,932
She knocks on the top bar of the gate.

352
00:13:03,932 --> 00:13:04,985
Three times.

353
00:13:04,985 --> 00:13:06,973
Then a fourth time, softer.

354
00:13:06,973 --> 00:13:08,819
The Doorman lifts his

355
00:13:08,819 --> 00:13:10,177
head toward the sound.

356
00:13:10,177 --> 00:13:12,506
Then he takes his hands off the gate,

357
00:13:12,506 --> 00:13:15,924
and walks inside, one step behind the night driver,

358
00:13:15,924 --> 00:13:19,361
the way he has been since day 190.

359
00:13:19,361 --> 00:13:21,376
Nora lets go of the rope.

360
00:13:21,376 --> 00:13:22,793
The gate swings shut.

361
00:13:22,793 --> 00:13:24,124
The bolt drops.

362
00:13:24,610 --> 00:13:27,182
"Welcome home," she says.

363
00:13:27,182 --> 00:13:28,457
On day 316,

364
00:13:28,457 --> 00:13:31,242
at sunset, somebody has to switch it off.

365
00:13:31,663 --> 00:13:32,839
By late afternoon,

366
00:13:32,839 --> 00:13:34,995
Wes has no voice left at all.

367
00:13:35,305 --> 00:13:37,470
So he holds the radio up to the microphone,

368
00:13:37,470 --> 00:13:40,084
and on the hill, Kit reads out an

369
00:13:40,084 --> 00:13:42,831
old bus timetable, stop by stop,

370
00:13:42,831 --> 00:13:46,057
and the loudspeaker carries it down into the yard.

371
00:13:46,057 --> 00:13:47,737
If it keeps calling all night,

372
00:13:47,737 --> 00:13:50,156
it will call every dead thing for miles.

373
00:13:50,156 --> 00:13:51,909
And the switch is down under

374
00:13:51,909 --> 00:13:53,889
the edge of the canopy,

375
00:13:53,889 --> 00:13:55,998
over the heads of the whole river.

376
00:13:55,998 --> 00:13:56,901
Wes goes.

377
00:13:57,339 --> 00:13:59,557
Nobody could stop him if they tried.

378
00:13:59,557 --> 00:14:01,763
He crawls along the canopy roof,

379
00:14:01,763 --> 00:14:03,201
flat on his stomach,

380
00:14:03,201 --> 00:14:06,589
to the very edge, right above the switch.

381
00:14:06,589 --> 00:14:09,083
Below him, thousands of faces are

382
00:14:09,083 --> 00:14:11,202
turned up toward the loudspeaker,

383
00:14:11,202 --> 00:14:14,454
mouths open, hands lifted, as if they are

384
00:14:14,454 --> 00:14:17,388
all waiting for one more announcement.

385
00:14:17,388 --> 00:14:18,739
Wes reaches down.

386
00:14:18,739 --> 00:14:21,319
His fingers find the switch.

387
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:21,965
Click.

388
00:14:21,965 --> 00:14:22,795
Silence.

389
00:14:22,795 --> 00:14:26,022
Real silence, the kind that has weight.

390
00:14:26,022 --> 00:14:27,575
And then nothing at all.

391
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:29,670
The river stands in the yard,

392
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:31,937
exactly where the last sound left it,

393
00:14:31,937 --> 00:14:32,948
facing the canopy,

394
00:14:32,948 --> 00:14:36,123
waiting for a voice that is never going to come back.

395
00:14:36,610 --> 00:14:38,185
Wes crawls back along the

396
00:14:38,185 --> 00:14:39,760
roof and onto the gantry.

397
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,108
Over the gate,

398
00:14:41,108 --> 00:14:44,001
he stops, takes the strip of tape off his sleeve,

399
00:14:44,001 --> 00:14:46,345
and very neatly tapes the bolt shut.

400
00:14:46,345 --> 00:14:48,572
Then he climbs over the wall and

401
00:14:48,572 --> 00:14:52,225
down Bram's ladder into the empty street.

402
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:55,482
From day 317 to day 323,

403
00:14:55,482 --> 00:14:57,859
you live with a view.

404
00:14:57,859 --> 00:15:00,434
The hill people give you a long room

405
00:15:00,434 --> 00:15:03,416
with big windows at the top of their hill.

406
00:15:03,416 --> 00:15:06,259
They offered you a place up here

407
00:15:06,259 --> 00:15:09,197
back on day 64, and you said no.

408
00:15:09,197 --> 00:15:12,389
A bunker for a view, Wes called it.

409
00:15:12,389 --> 00:15:14,138
Now you have the view.

410
00:15:14,138 --> 00:15:17,062
From the window, you can see the depot.

411
00:15:17,062 --> 00:15:17,976
The canopy.

412
00:15:17,976 --> 00:15:19,272
The solar panel.

413
00:15:19,272 --> 00:15:21,542
The yard, full again,

414
00:15:21,542 --> 00:15:25,332
wall to wall, quiet as a field of wheat with no wind.

415
00:15:25,332 --> 00:15:27,024
And over the street,

416
00:15:27,024 --> 00:15:29,360
the sign, swinging a little.

417
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,565
FOUR ALIVE.

418
00:15:30,565 --> 00:15:33,065
Over a yard full of the dead.

419
00:15:33,504 --> 00:15:35,511
You've never seen anything that

420
00:15:35,511 --> 00:15:37,679
looked so much like home and so

421
00:15:37,679 --> 00:15:40,193
little like it at the same time.

422
00:15:40,193 --> 00:15:41,388
Every sunset,

423
00:15:41,388 --> 00:15:44,743
Nora says Still here into the radio.

424
00:15:44,743 --> 00:15:46,958
Every sunset, Ansel answers.

425
00:15:46,958 --> 00:15:48,758
"Bridge is ours.

426
00:15:48,758 --> 00:15:49,758
Again."

427
00:15:49,758 --> 00:15:51,969
On day 320,

428
00:15:51,969 --> 00:15:54,763
Kit asks why the sign still says four.

429
00:15:54,763 --> 00:15:56,660
"Because we're not

430
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:57,905
there anymore," says Nora.

431
00:15:57,905 --> 00:16:00,024
"We'll change it when we're somewhere."

432
00:16:00,896 --> 00:16:04,092
Every night, after Nora says Still here,

433
00:16:04,092 --> 00:16:06,120
Ruth takes the radio and turns it

434
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:08,266
slowly to another frequency,

435
00:16:08,266 --> 00:16:11,599
and says the same thing into it, again and again.

436
00:16:12,214 --> 00:16:13,924
"Point, Point, this is Ruth.

437
00:16:13,924 --> 00:16:15,018
Do you read?"

438
00:16:15,986 --> 00:16:17,641
Nobody ever answers.

439
00:16:17,641 --> 00:16:19,802
She sits with it in her lap

440
00:16:19,802 --> 00:16:22,806
until Kit falls asleep against her shoulder,

441
00:16:22,806 --> 00:16:25,529
and then a little longer.

442
00:16:25,529 --> 00:16:28,164
From day 324 to day 329,

443
00:16:28,164 --> 00:16:31,163
you think about the sea.

444
00:16:31,713 --> 00:16:33,455
There is a list on the wall of

445
00:16:33,455 --> 00:16:36,128
the long room now, in Wes's writing.

446
00:16:36,128 --> 00:16:37,366
Things we'd take.

447
00:16:37,366 --> 00:16:38,879
The first thing on it

448
00:16:38,879 --> 00:16:41,369
is still the orange bag.

449
00:16:41,369 --> 00:16:42,659
Seven people.

450
00:16:42,659 --> 00:16:45,705
One truck with a cab built for three.

451
00:16:45,705 --> 00:16:47,410
Two days of roads that

452
00:16:47,410 --> 00:16:49,801
nobody has driven for a year.

453
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:52,895
"We need something bigger," says Ruth.

454
00:16:52,895 --> 00:16:55,719
Bram looks out of the big window,

455
00:16:55,719 --> 00:16:56,722
down at the depot,

456
00:16:56,722 --> 00:17:00,177
at the dark rectangle in the middle of the full yard

457
00:17:00,177 --> 00:17:02,316
where something bigger used to stand.

458
00:17:02,316 --> 00:17:04,101
He whistles two notes.

459
00:17:04,101 --> 00:17:06,176
Then, slowly, a third.

460
00:17:06,176 --> 00:17:07,350
"That means

461
00:17:07,350 --> 00:17:09,860
maybe," says Kit.

462
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:13,447
On day 327, Ansel calls with news.

463
00:17:13,447 --> 00:17:16,242
He has sent two of his people along

464
00:17:16,242 --> 00:17:18,500
the farm tracks to look at the gravel pit.

465
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,609
The water has gone

466
00:17:19,609 --> 00:17:21,308
back down into the gravel.

467
00:17:21,308 --> 00:17:23,876
The slope of mud is drying in the sun.

468
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,886
The pit is almost empty.

469
00:17:26,724 --> 00:17:27,399
"Almost?"

470
00:17:27,399 --> 00:17:28,327
says Vera.

471
00:17:28,327 --> 00:17:31,104
"There are a few dozen left

472
00:17:31,104 --> 00:17:32,618
at the bottom," says Ansel.

473
00:17:32,618 --> 00:17:34,982
"Stuck in the mud around the coach.

474
00:17:34,982 --> 00:17:37,547
They don't seem to want to go anywhere."

475
00:17:37,547 --> 00:17:38,907
Vera turns the travel

476
00:17:38,907 --> 00:17:40,658
alarm clock over in her hands.

477
00:17:40,658 --> 00:17:42,145
It is still ticking.

478
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:44,005
"The coach," she says.

479
00:17:44,005 --> 00:17:45,978
"Is it still standing up?"

480
00:17:46,463 --> 00:17:48,067
"It's still standing up."

481
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,151
Vera says nothing else.

482
00:17:50,151 --> 00:17:51,211
But that night,

483
00:17:51,211 --> 00:17:55,626
she sleeps lying down, for the first time in a year.

484
00:17:55,626 --> 00:17:56,590
On day 330,

485
00:17:56,590 --> 00:17:59,416
the radio speaks with a new voice.

486
00:17:59,416 --> 00:18:00,286
Late at night.

487
00:18:00,286 --> 00:18:02,547
Everybody is asleep except Kit,

488
00:18:02,547 --> 00:18:04,501
who sits by the radio every night now,

489
00:18:04,501 --> 00:18:06,036
the way Nora used to.

490
00:18:06,036 --> 00:18:08,325
And so it is Kit who hears it first,

491
00:18:08,325 --> 00:18:10,647
through the hiss, very faint,

492
00:18:10,647 --> 00:18:13,671
as if it is coming from the bottom of the sea.

493
00:18:14,366 --> 00:18:14,868
"Ruth.

494
00:18:14,868 --> 00:18:17,043
Ruth, if you can hear me.

495
00:18:17,043 --> 00:18:18,180
It's Tam."

496
00:18:18,635 --> 00:18:21,362
Kit grabs the radio with both hands.

497
00:18:21,362 --> 00:18:22,031
"Dad!"

498
00:18:22,548 --> 00:18:23,975
Everybody is awake now.

499
00:18:23,975 --> 00:18:25,403
Ruth is across the room

500
00:18:25,403 --> 00:18:26,694
before you can blink,

501
00:18:26,694 --> 00:18:29,418
her yellow raincoat over her nightclothes.

502
00:18:30,016 --> 00:18:31,402
"Kit," says the voice,

503
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:33,317
and it cracks in the middle.

504
00:18:33,317 --> 00:18:35,056
Then it steadies.

505
00:18:35,056 --> 00:18:36,051
"Listen to me.

506
00:18:36,051 --> 00:18:36,975
Both of you.

507
00:18:36,975 --> 00:18:38,696
Put your mother on."

508
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:40,866
"I'm here," says Ruth.

509
00:18:40,866 --> 00:18:44,109
"They're coming down the beach," says Tam.

510
00:18:44,109 --> 00:18:45,944
"Not a few dozen.

511
00:18:45,944 --> 00:18:46,782
Hundreds.

512
00:18:46,782 --> 00:18:49,009
More every low tide.

513
00:18:49,009 --> 00:18:51,018
They walk out on the road and they

514
00:18:51,018 --> 00:18:52,541
stand at our gate,

515
00:18:52,541 --> 00:18:56,154
and the sea pushes them back, and they come again.

516
00:18:56,154 --> 00:18:58,509
The gate is leaning, Ruth."

517
00:18:59,125 --> 00:19:00,844
Ruth closes her eyes.

518
00:19:00,844 --> 00:19:03,166
"And in five weeks," says Tam,

519
00:19:03,166 --> 00:19:04,957
"it's the spring tide.

520
00:19:04,957 --> 00:19:07,310
The lowest water of the year.

521
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:09,476
The road will be dry for half a day.

522
00:19:09,802 --> 00:19:12,076
They'll have all the time in the world."

523
00:19:12,076 --> 00:19:14,080
Then the hiss swallows him,

524
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,878
and he's gone.

525
00:19:15,878 --> 00:19:17,377
Three hundred and thirty days.

526
00:19:17,816 --> 00:19:19,436
The same orange bandage.

527
00:19:19,436 --> 00:19:21,810
Nora is holding the flashlight.

528
00:19:22,153 --> 00:19:24,711
You are holding the orange bag.

529
00:19:24,711 --> 00:19:26,798
Tomorrow is day 331.

530
00:19:26,798 --> 00:19:30,043
The river is home in your yard,

531
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,665
the bolt is taped shut,

532
00:19:31,665 --> 00:19:34,769
and the bridge belongs to the living again.

533
00:19:34,769 --> 00:19:37,180
But two days away, at the end of a

534
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:39,729
beach on a postcard, there is a door

535
00:19:39,729 --> 00:19:43,019
the sea opens by itself, twice a day.

536
00:19:43,019 --> 00:19:44,125
In five weeks,

537
00:19:44,125 --> 00:19:47,447
it will open wider than it has all year.

538
00:19:47,447 --> 00:19:48,624
And the dead are

539
00:19:48,624 --> 00:19:50,495
already waiting in front of it.

540
00:19:50,495 --> 00:19:51,563
Would you have given

541
00:19:51,563 --> 00:19:53,084
your home to the horde?

542
00:19:53,457 --> 00:19:54,714
Would you go to the sea,

543
00:19:54,714 --> 00:19:56,113
or stay on the hill?

544
00:19:56,646 --> 00:19:58,191
Tell us in the comments,

545
00:19:58,191 --> 00:20:00,252
and subscribe to Last Safe Door,

546
00:20:00,252 --> 00:20:03,024
so you're here for day 331.
